---
source: tests/doctor.rs
expression: r.stdout
---
ricepilot doctor: 4 problems. nothing was changed; the commands are for you to run.

PROBLEM 1 of 4: <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/journal/current.toml
  an operation was interrupted and has not been recovered.
  rule: SAFETY.md R5 (never half-applied); DESIGN.md §7, rung 2

  a switch or a rollback into profile `new` (id <TS>) wrote this journal and did not
  retire it, so it may have stopped part way. it touches:
    <HOME>/.config/hypr
    <HOME>/.config/foot
    <HOME>/.config/btop

  if another ricepilot is running right now, this is its journal: let it
  finish and run doctor again. otherwise `recover` reads every destination
  and finishes or undoes the operation as a whole, never half of it. until
  then, what follows may describe a half-finished state.

  run:
    # see what recovery would do; this changes nothing
    ricepilot recover
    ricepilot recover --commit

PROBLEM 2 of 4: <HOME>/.config/foot
  is a real directory, not the link ricepilot recorded.
  rule: SAFETY.md, the ownership predicate; NOT-POSSIBLE.md#real-dir-at-managed-dest

  the ledger recorded a link here to
    <HOME>/rice/new/foot
  for profile `new`.

  this is what a rice installer does — caelestia's install.fish and
  `caelestia install` turn links back into directories — and whatever
  it wrote is in there. every switch refuses this path until it is
  resolved, because re-linking it would strand that.

  run:
    # what is in it, against the tree the link pointed into
    diff -r <HOME>/rice/new/foot <HOME>/.config/foot
    # set it aside (nothing is lost), then put the link back
    mv -nT <HOME>/.config/foot <HOME>/.config/foot.set-aside
    ricepilot plan new
    ricepilot switch new --commit

PROBLEM 3 of 4: <HOME>/rice/new
  profile `new`'s tree has changed since it was recorded.
  rule: SAFETY.md R7; D34

  1 path has changed since ricepilot recorded it at <TS>:
    changed      hypr/marker

  this is the profile linked now, so these changes are what the next login
  loads.

  ricepilot never writes into a profile; an app, a script or an editor did.
  paths an app rewrites on its own belong in `volatile`.

  run:
    ricepilot verify new

PROBLEM 4 of 4: <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/rescue.sh
  cannot be relied on.
  rule: DESIGN.md §7, rung 3; D37

  `sh -n` rejects it:
    <what sh said>

  it is not a script ricepilot wrote.

  it is rung 3 of the recovery ladder, the one for a TTY when nothing else
  works. do not rely on it as it is.

  run:
    sh -n <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/rescue.sh
    # rung 1 of the ladder still works; see what it would do
    ricepilot rollback
    # the next `switch` or `rollback --commit` writes the script again

not checked, or worth knowing:
  - profile `new`: <HOME>/rice/new/hypr/hyprland.lua is a Lua config, which nothing can check before a login (NOT-POSSIBLE.md#verify-lua-config)
  - profile `old`: <HOME>/rice/old/hypr/hyprland.lua is a Lua config, which nothing can check before a login (NOT-POSSIBLE.md#verify-lua-config)
  - profile `old`: no manifest has been recorded for it yet, so its tree was not compared with anything
  - running theme daemons (/proc) and snapper's configuration (/etc/snapper) were not checked: this is the test sandbox (D56)

ok: 2 owned links intact; the ledger and the manifests agree; 2 hypr trees have an entry file; attic: 1 entry, 0 B (the newest, <TS>, 0 B); no verify-config copies; no interrupted gc
